WEBVTT

00:00:00.102 --> 00:00:05.283
This is a classic SQL trap The query asks for
records whose

00:00:05.309 --> 00:00:09.395
payment status is not in a list containing Paid and
null At

00:00:09.421 --> 00:00:13.700
first that may look reasonable But a null inside the
NOT IN

00:00:13.725 --> 00:00:17.475
list can cause comparisons that appear to be
non-matches to become UNKNOWN

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:21.689
The database cannot prove that a value is different
from an unknown

00:00:21.702 --> 00:00:27.361
list element Run the example in the browser and
observe the result

00:00:28.786 --> 00:00:33.400
Then copy it into pgAdmin if you want to test
variations For

00:00:33.413 --> 00:00:38.130
example remove null from the list and compare the
output The safer

00:00:38.156 --> 00:00:40.875
approach is normally to keep null out of the list
and handle

00:00:40.888 --> 00:00:43.761
missing values explicitly according to the business
rule
